**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitContentFileJsonTests`

**How to implement.** An experiment persists as its own kit file, `<name>.experiment-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema (001 §A 'Kit extensions … .experiment-json', 'A file that exists many times is named by its own identity'; the S4.3 brief: each kit file kind has a JSON schema and a schema version and is written atomically through KitProxy, and until S8.3 / S9.1 give experiments template names the name is its ExperimentId, e.g. `E3`; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 124's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`); no second parser or writer is written. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (a) `ExperimentId` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentId`) gains `member this.fileStem : FileStem`, `FileStem.ofText` (step 24) of `E<n>`, so `ExperimentId 3` is stored as `E3.experiment-json`. (b) After `Experiment` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`): `ExperimentFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; experiment : Experiment }`, the `.experiment-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1. `type Experiment with member this.experimentFile : ExperimentFile` is the experiment at the current schema version. A file is read back as its `experiment` field; no member converts the other way (ELEV006). (2) Schema. New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/experiment.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/kit.schema.json` (step 124), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/experiment.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Only under `if` it is 1 (`then`): the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `experiment` (`additionalProperties: false`); `experiment` holds exactly `id` (a positive integer), `setup` (an array), `varied`, `measurement`, `range` (an object), `dataFileOpt` and `sourceWaveLengthOpt`; `dataFileOpt` is `null` or an object holding exactly `path` (a non-empty string) and `contentHash` (the content-hash definition of `library-common.schema.json`, step 30, referenced by its `$id`). The descriptors, bindings, range and wavelength are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one, as step 30's payloads are. A file of another version therefore passes the schema and reaches the typed version check. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/kit.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateExperimentFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith` (step 29), its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateKitFile` (step 124) does. (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs`, `module KitContentFiles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `KitFolderStore.fs` (step 124): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines: the kit's content files, their texts and their typed reads and writes (spec 0050 S4.3). (a) `type ExperimentFile with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` is `nodeOf this` (step 27) rendered by `canonicalFileText` (step 124): indented canonical JSON, LF line ends, one final `\n`. (b) `type KitFileText with member this.parseExperimentFile : Result<ExperimentFile, StorageError>` is `parseVersionedText validateExperimentFile ExperimentKitFile.extension ExperimentFile.currentSchemaVersion this.value` (steps 123, 124). There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitContentFileJsonTests.fs`, `module KitContentFileJsonTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its fixtures are two test-local experiments written as records, as `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs` writes its E1 / E2 / E3: E1 varies a polarizer's R1 over a setup binding the 1 mm glass plate sample by its version 1 (`BoundByVersion`), the 600 nm source preset by its entry id (`BoundByEntryId` of `PresetIds.source600`, step 20) and one `Unbound` element, carries a `DataAttachment` at `data/run 1.csv` with a test-local 64-character lowercase hex hash, and sets its source to 632.8 nm (`WaveLength.nm`); E3 is a dark line with no varied element, no attachment and no wavelength. `an experiment is stored under its id`: `(ExperimentId 3).fileStem` is `FileStem "E3"`, and `ExperimentKitFile.fileNameOf` of it is `FileName "E3.experiment-json"`. `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`: `experimentFile`, `fileText`, then `parseExperimentFile` answers an equal file for E1 and for E3; the text holds no `\r`, ends with exactly one `\n`, lists its top-level keys as `experiment` then `schemaVersion`, and writing the parsed file again gives the same text. `an experiment file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: E1's text with `schemaVersion` set to 2, with its body intact and as `{ "schemaVersion": 2 }` alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = ExperimentKitFile.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`. `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds`: E1's text without `experiment`, with an extra top-level key `notes`, with `experiment.id` set to 0, and with `dataFileOpt.contentHash` set to `abc`, each answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; the text `{` answers `MalformedJsonErr`.

**Acceptance.** After the experiment file lands, `ExperimentFile.fileText` MUST render canonical JSON that `KitFileText.parseExperimentFile` reads back equal, validated against `schema/experiment.schema.json`, another schema version being `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, and `ExperimentId.fileStem` MUST name an experiment `E<n>`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an experiment is stored under its id`, `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `an experiment file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.
